      "text": [
        "750 - وَ سُئِلَ اَلصَّادِقُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ: عَنْ قَوْلِ اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ لِمُوسَى عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ «۝ فَاخْلَعْ نَعْلَيْكَ إِنَّكَ بِالْوٰادِ اَلْمُقَدَّسِ طُوىً ۝»\nقَالَ «كَانَتَا مِنْ جِلْدِ حِمَارٍ مَيِّتٍ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.750 - Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) was asked about the verse in which Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic, said to Musa (as):\n\"Remove your sandals, for you are in the sacred valley of Tuwa\" (Surah Taha 20:12).\nImam (as) said: \"They were made from the skin of a dead donkey.\""
        ]
      }
